{
  "description": "The stored record of the favorites, docs/board/light-v1.md#stored-favorites. Each case lays out a record of 598 bytes: `header` is bytes 0 to 3, `entries` are written from byte 4, 99 bytes each (the id, the name as UTF-8 or `name_hex`, padded with 0 to 80 bytes, the 18-byte light record `look`), every other byte is 0, and `size` cuts or extends it. `favorites` and `start` are what is read, in the form of the protocol's `favorites` reply, `next_id` is byte 3 as read, and `damaged` says the record was refused (the ready-made favorites). With `round_trip`, writing what was read gives the same bytes.",
